cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Pledge
abstract: "Pledge is a small language for learning restricted dependent types, built so that you can see what its type checker knows at every point of a program. It runs entirely in the browser: an editor shows, beside the program, the expected type, the scope with what each entry is known to equal, the value constructors a match rules out with a derivation of why, and the parameters a recursive call has to decrease, together with a tutorial running from Nat to proofs about addition and multiplication. This repository holds its specification, an implementation in TypeScript, the tutorial, and a written (not machine-checked) argument that no program can prove False."
